            <ArticleTitle>Scimitar Syndrome-Complex Surgical Revision 3 Decades After Repair.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e183-e185</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-4975(16)30957-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2016.07.056</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a 39-year-old woman with scimitar syndrome who had a 2-patch repair 3 decades previously and presented with a right-to-left shunt of the inferior vena cava (IVC) to the left atrium resulting from baffle dehiscence. We discuss details of our reoperative repair.</AbstractText>
